\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces BP trap inventory: layer indices where $C(t)$ collapsed to $\approx 0.007$--$0.010$, and whether the trap recovered at the next layer. \emph  {Recovers}: correct value restored at layer $+1$. \emph  {Persistent}: final layer still trapped, no further chance to recover. MI60 runs (both QR modes) show more trapping than MI100 at the same $\chi $ due to floating-point non-determinism (MFMA on MI100 vs.\ vector FP on MI60). \emph  {n/a}: that $\chi $ was not run on this architecture/mode combination. No traps occur on the $5\times 5$ grid in either method.}}{16}{table.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:trap_inventory}{{3}{16}{BP trap inventory: layer indices where $\Ct $ collapsed to $\approx 0.007$--$0.010$, and whether the trap recovered at the next layer. \emph {Recovers}: correct value restored at layer $+1$. \emph {Persistent}: final layer still trapped, no further chance to recover. MI60 runs (both QR modes) show more trapping than MI100 at the same $\chi $ due to floating-point non-determinism (MFMA on MI100 vs.\ vector FP on MI60). \emph {n/a}: that $\chi $ was not run on this architecture/mode combination. No traps occur on the $5\times 5$ grid in either method}{table.caption.18}{}}
